[86.493283, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b]133;C\u001b\\\r\u001b]666;vte.shell.preexec!\u001b\\"]
[113.628603, "o", "**QSIPrep does not have an `--output-spaces` flag**, and there is no flag to write preprocessed DWI in MNI152NLin2009cAsym space.\r\n\r\nPer `pages/entity/concept-output-spaces.md` (lines 57, 75–79):\r\n\r\n> QSIPrep outputs DWI in **`space-ACPC` only** (hard-coded). `--output-spaces` is **not** a QSIPrep CLI option. The T1w↔MNI152NLin2009cAsym warps are computed and emitted as `.h5` xfm files so downstream consumers can warp scalar/tractography derivatives into MNI space, but the preprocessed DWI image itself is never resampled into MNI by QSIPrep. `--output-resolution` controls the ACPC voxel size — that is the only spatial-output flag QSIPrep exposes.\r\n\r\nIn other words, after QSIPrep you apply the emitted `*_from-T1w_to-MNI152NLin2009cAsym_mode-image_xfm.h5` yourself if you need MNI-space DWI. The wiki notes explicitly that earlier claims that QSIPrep \"iterates over multiple output spaces\" were hallucinated and have been corrected.\r\n"]
[113.628964, "o", "\u001b[?1006l\u001b[?1003l\u001b[?1002l\u001b[?1000l\u001b(B\u000f\u001b[>4m\u001b[<u\u001b[?1004l"]
[113.629077, "o", "\u001b[?2031l\u001b[?2004l\u001b[?25h\u001b7\u001b[r\u001b8"]
